[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65096,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seborrhoeic keratosis is a benign lesion characterized by proliferation of the parabasal cells of the squamous epithelium.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65097,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65098,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F21.0 Seborrhoeic keratosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65099,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> senile wart; seborrhoeic wart</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65100,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65101,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seborrhoeic keratosis arises in the hair-bearing skin of the vulva, intertriginous areas, and inner side of thighs. Some lesions with seborrhoeic keratosis&ndash;like features were recently also reported in the cervix and vagina {27792064}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65102,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are asymptomatic, raised, maculopapular, nodular or plaque-like, and often pigmented lesions.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65103,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seborrhoeic keratosis can be seen in all age groups.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65104,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most seborrhoeic keratoses, particularly in young women, are associated with genital-type low-risk HPV infection {22583360} and should be considered to be condyloma acuminatum. However, HPV is not identified in a significant proportion of cases in elderly patients. Such cases probably represent conventional, non-genital seborrhoeic keratosis involving the vulva, although low&ndash;copy-number HPV infection in older patients cannot be excluded {24556611}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65105,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In younger women, these lesions are more likely to be condyloma acuminatum.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65106,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seborrhoeic keratoses are raised, waxy, maculopapular, nodular or plaque-like, and often pigmented lesions with a so-called stuck-on appearance.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65107,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions display an acanthotic epidermis with variable papillomatosis, hyperkeratosis, and no significant nuclear atypia; they may have areas of morphology overlapping with that of condyloma acuminatum. Usually, pseudohorn cysts (intralesional cysts of loose keratin) are easily identified. HPV positivity by in&nbsp;situ hybridization and/or PCR supports a diagnosis of condyloma acuminatum simulating seborrhoeic keratosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65108,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65109,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65110,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> acanthosis; papillomatosis; hyperkeratosis with keratin-filled horn cysts; absence of significant atypia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65111,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65112,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 370,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are benign lesions.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:07:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]